<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="description" content="Nunjucks engine — context-aware escaping across HTML, attribute, and script auto-tojson zones.">
  <title>{{ appName }} — Security Features</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; max-width: 880px; margin: 60px auto; padding: 0 24px; color: #2c3e50; line-height: 1.6; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 1.6rem; }
    h2 { color: #3498db; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 32px; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    .raw, .safe { padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 6px 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 0.85rem; word-break: break-all; }
    .raw { background: #fde8e8; border-left: 4px solid #e74c3c; }
    .safe { background: #e8f6f3; border-left: 4px solid #27ae60; }
    code { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; background: #f3f4f6; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
    .script-output { background: #2c3e50; color: #ecf0f1; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
    a { color: #3498db; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Security Features</h1>
  <p>Auto-escaping inspects the <em>output context</em> — the same value lands safely in HTML, in an attribute, or as a JS literal. The engine never trusts the context to be what the developer assumed.</p>

  <h2>1. Context-aware escaping — HTML</h2>
  <div class="raw">direct: {{ userInput }}</div>
  <div class="safe">escaped: {{ userInput |> sanitize }}</div>

  <h2>2. Script context — auto-toJSON</h2>
  <p>Inside <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>, plain values are JSON-encoded automatically. The output is a valid JS literal — no string-injection surface.</p>
  <script>
    const config = {{ configData }};
    console.log('Config loaded:', config);
  </script>
  <div class="script-output">const config = {{ configData }};</div>

  <h2>3. Context-aware escaping — attribute</h2>
  <p>Attribute values get quote-aware escaping.</p>
  <div class="raw">direct: {{ attrContent }}</div>
  <div class="safe">in-attr: &lt;div data-value="{{ attrContent }}"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</div>

  <p><a href="/">← Back to index</a></p>
</body>
</html>